"Serving Runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, CaKit) for model execution\").\n76\tIt is treated as in-platform; the missing dedicated context file is logged as a\n77\thealth warning, not provisioned as a new component (Rule 20 onboarding chains\n78\tdo not apply — the runtimes already exist in the platform).\n79\t\n80\t## Step 3 — Investigation Epics\n81\t\n82\tThe strategy's Open Questions section states \"None — the convention work\n83\t(HLR-1) is prerequisite design, and per-component adoptions are mechanical\n84\tonce it lands.\" No open questions, pending reviews, conditional ADRs, or risks\n85\tare declared anywhere else in the strategy. No genuine unknowns exist that\n86\twould change which epics exist or what they do. Therefore: **no Investigation\n87\tepics, no conditional branches.**\n88\t\n89\tThe convention itself (HLR-1) is prerequisite *design work that produces an\n90\tartifact*, i.e., an Implementation epic — not an Investigation. The strategy\n91\tauthor has already made that classification.\n92\t\n93\t## Step 4 — HLR to Epic Mapping\n94\t\n95\tEach HLR maps to exactly one epic except HLR-3, which spans two components\n96\t(KServe controller, Serving Runtimes) and maps to two epics. No epic carries\n97\tHLRs at multiple priority levels, so no priority splits are required — the\n98\tstrategy already priority-levels the adoptions per component, and each\n99\tadoption is independently deferrable by design (\"Component adoptions are\n100\tindependent of each other once the convention exists\").\n101\t\n102\tPriority inheritance: the convention epic (E001) blocks all P0 adoptions and\n103\tis itself P0 via HLR-1. The docs-authoring epic is exempt from priority\n104\tinheritance (Step 4 exception): strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1.\n105\t\n106\t## Epic List\n107\t\n108\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n109\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n110\t| E001 | Platform structured logging convention | Implementation | RHOAI Platform | P0 |\n111\t| E002 | Dashboard structured logging adoption | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n112\t| E003 | KServe controller structured logging adoption | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n113\t| E004 | Serving runtimes structured logging adoption | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n114\t| E005 | Data Science Pipelines structured logging adoption | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n115\t| E006 | Model Registry structured logging adoption | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n116\t| E007 | TrustyAI structured logging adoption | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n117\t| E008 | Notebooks controller structured logging adoption | Implementation | Workbenches | P1 |\n118\t| E009 | Training Operator structured logging adoption | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n119\t| E010 | Structured logging documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n120\t\n121\t## Dependency DAG\n122\t\n123\t```mermaid\n124\tgraph TD\n125\t    E001[E001 convention] --> E002[Dashboard]\n126\t    E001 --> E003[KServe controller]\n127\t    E001 --> E004[Serving runtimes]\n128\t    E001 --> E005[DSP]\n129\t    E001 --> E006[Model Registry]\n130\t    E001 --> E007[TrustyAI]\n131\t    E001 --> E008[Notebooks]\n132\t    E001 --> E009[Training Operator]\n133\t    E002 --> E010[Documentation]\n134\t    E003 --> E010\n135\t    E004 --> E010\n136\t    E005 --> E010\n137\t    E006 --> E010\n138\t    E007 --> E010\n139\t    E008 --> E010\n140\t    E009 --> E010\n141\t    E001 --> E010\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\t## DAG Justification\n145\t\n146\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n147\t|---|---|---|\n148\t| E001 → E002…E009 | 13 (artifact consumers build against) | The convention (JSON schema, required fields, per-language library guidance) is the artifact each adoption's code builds against. The strategy states adoptions are possible only \"once the convention exists\". |\n149\t| E001…E009 → E010 | 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes the log format and example queries for what was built; it must reflect the published convention and the actual component adoptions. |\n150\t| (none among E002…E009) | 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | Strategy: \"Component adoptions are independent of each other once the convention exists.\" Each touches a distinct component/repo. |\n151\t| (no konflux/repo/license onboarding edges) | 20 N/A | All components already exist in the platform and in the canonical component list; KServe is noted \"Konflux onboarded: yes\" in its architecture context. |\n152\t\n153\tRule 25 note: no `konflux-onboarding` epic exists in any dependency chain, so\n154\tno \"build pipeline green\" AC is added.\n155\t\n156\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n157\t\n158\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n159\t|---|---|---|\n160\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 |\n161\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 |\n162\t| HLR-3 | P0 | E003, E004 |\n163\t| HLR-4 | P1 | E005 |\n164\t| HLR-5 | P1 | E006 |\n165\t| HLR-6 | P1 | E007 |\n166\t| HLR-7 | P1 | E008 |\n167\t| HLR-8 | P2 | E009 |\n168\t| HLR-9 | P2 | E010 |\n169\t\n170\tAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without an HLR.\n171\t\n172\t## Health Warnings\n173\t\n174\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Impacted Teams, Dependencies\n175\t   table, Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), and NFRs are absent. Owning\n176\t   teams were derived from architecture-context files; per-epic acceptance\n177\t   criteria were derived from HLRs and the problem statement. A convention\n178\t   owner (\"RHOAI Platform\" / Platform Operator component) was inferred —\n179\t   confirm the owning team before scheduling.\n180\t2. **Serving Runtimes architecture-context gap**: no dedicated\n181\t   architecture-context file exists for Serving Runtimes; its presence in the\n182\t   platform is corroborated only by the KServe context file's dependency\n183\t   listing (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit). Flag for architecture-context coverage.\n184\t3. **Serving runtimes upstream risk**: the serving runtimes