ds: timestamp, level, component,\n54\t  namespace, correlation id (correlation id populated wherever request context\n55\t  is available).\n56\t- A single user request can be followed through Dashboard logs using the\n57\t  correlation id alone, with no Dashboard-specific parsing rules.\n58\t- The log format change is revertible (configuration flag or documented\n59\t  rollback path) so existing log consumers are not broken during transition.\n60\t- No diagnostic information present in the previous log output is lost.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P0): Dashboard emits convention-conformant logs.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b69366d046e540a8","agent_id":"a8984966aa8d6a829","session_id":"0fdcac5b-f320-4d39-9898-d6f62ea52db6","uuid":"57934acf-c2b0-4a6d-80c3-f3450eaf89f8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:09:26.842Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adab64cb256eb32e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
