{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bac602930e62802","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9011-E004\n3\ttitle: Serving runtimes structured logging adoption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9011\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9011-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Serving runtimes structured logging adoption\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThe RHOAI serving runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit) emit convention-conformant\n35\tstructured JSON logs, so model serving request logs can be correlated with the\n36\tsame request observed in the Dashboard and elsewhere in the platform.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Bring each serving runtime's log output into conformance with the published\n41\t  platform logging convention, following the convention's library guidance for\n42\t  each runtime's language.\n43\t- Populate the required fields — timestamp, level, component, namespace, and\n44\t  correlation id — on every emitted record, propagating the correlation id\n45\t  from inference request context where available.\n46\t- Preserve existing diagnostic content.\n47\t\n48\t## Assumptions and Risks\n49\t\n50\t- The serving runtimes are upstream projects consumed by the platform.\n51\t  Adoption is expected to land via the existing midstream change process; if\n52\t  midstream patching proves untenable for a runtime, upstream coordination\n53\t  may be required — the strategy characterizes all adoptions as mechanical,\n54\t  and this assumption should be revisited if it does not hold.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Logs emitted by each serving runtime are valid JSON records conforming to\n59\t  the platform logging convention schema.\n60\t- Every record carries the required fields: timestamp, level, component,\n61\t  namespace, correlation id (correlation id populated wherever inference\n62\t  request context is available).\n63\t- A model serving request can be correlated across Dashboard and serving\n64\t  runtime logs using the correlation id alone.\n65\t- The log format change is revertible (configuration flag or documented\n66\t  rollback path) so existing log consumers are not broken during transition.\n67\t- No diagnostic information present in the previous log output is lost.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-3 (P0, serving runtimes portion): KServe controller and serving\n72\t  runtimes emit convention-conformant logs.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b69366d046e540a8","agent_id":"a8984966aa8d6a829","session_id":"0fdcac5b-f320-4d39-9898-d6f62ea52db6","uuid":"63b21001-79ea-4a64-a39c-6025c135b929","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:09:28.433Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bac602930e62802","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
