g (2/2)\n108\t\n109\tAll ten epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (not\n110\t`investigation_signals`); all ten ai-signals rationale files exist and their\n111\tvalues match frontmatter. Spot-checks hold up well: E001's conservative\n112\tscores (existing_foundation 0 for greenfield convention, open_questions 0\n113\tbecause the design decisions are the work itself, repo_access 0 with no\n114\tpublication location named, human_process_gates -1 for cross-team sign-off)\n115\tare each justified; E004's external_dependency 0 and architecture_claims 0\n116\tare grounded in the real upstream/context-file gaps; E010's\n117\thuman_process_gates -1 reflects the docs review process. Per instructions,\n118\tcomputed `ai_implementability` values were not re-derived.\n119\t\n120\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n121\t\n122\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLRs. Rule-mandated ACs are\n123\tpresent on every epic that meets the rule's criteria: all nine replacement\n124\tepics (E001–E009 where they replace log output — E002 through E009) carry the\n125\trevertibility/rollback AC, and the docs-authoring epic E010 carries the\n126\ttechnical-review AC. No konflux chain exists, so the Rule 25 build-pipeline\n127\tAC correctly does not apply. No epic body references sibling epics by draft\n128\tID (E001 etc.); cross-epic references use the convention/component names.\n129\t\n130\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n131\t\n132\tAll strategy scope is covered: all 9 HLRs, the correlation-id propagation\n133\tgoal from the problem statement (per-epic ACs plus the docs example-query\n134\tAC), and HLR-9 documentation via the docs-authoring epic E010. Out-of-scope\n135\titems (log storage/forwarding, metrics/tracing) are correctly excluded.\n136\tStrategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: the serving-runtimes\n137\tupstream risk appears as an explicit Assumptions and Risks section on E004,\n138\tand the missing-strategy-sections and context